  "description": "YEXTII crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C162 H124 N12 O16 Tb4,C2 H3 N1,C1 H2 Cl2. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.578-3.873 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.39-111.42°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C165H129Cl2N13O16Tb4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
